docs/release.md (last touched at k18/k19, before v0.1.0 shipped) still reads as
first-time bootstrap: step 1 "Create the GitHub repo Getty/skilletor and push main" (already
done - origin exists, tags v0.1.0/v0.1.1 exist), step 4 hardcodes `git tag v0.1.0`, and the
"Marketplace entry (add to Getty/marketplace)" JSON block is the text that went in for v0.1.0,
already added - nothing marks it done or shows how to update it for a later release.

For v0.2.0 the doc gives no guidance: whether the GitHub repo/CI/marketplace-entry steps are
one-time (skip them) or need re-verification, and what the tag command should say this time.
It also does not mention checking the marketplace entry description against the current
plugin.json as part of a release (see the sibling ticket on that drift).

Rework into a repeatable release checklist: split one-time bootstrap (repo creation, first
marketplace entry, CI setup) from what repeats every release (version bump in package.json +
both plugin.json, tag matching, dist rebuilt, README/SKILL.md CLI reference review,
marketplace description still matching plugin.json). Audit-only per house rules - the
release-checker/worker prep the text, the maintainer edits docs/release.md, Getty/marketplace
and tags/pushes.
